/* Generated by tools/make-prose.py from the printed character sheet. Do not edit by hand. */
(function(){var E=window.SheetEngine||(window.SheetEngine={});E.PROSE={"feats": "<p>Racial (Moon elf, alternate features): Low-Light Vision; Keen Senses (+2 Perception); Silver-Tongued Diplomacy (+2 Diplomacy and Bluff, 1 extra language; replaces Elven Magic); Wanderer&#x27;s Stride (+5 ft speed, ignores natural difficult terrain; replaces Elven Weapon Familiarity); Moonlight Resilience (cold resistance 5; light or dancing lights 1/day, no burnout; replaces Elven Immunities).</p><p>Traits: Reactionary (Combat): +2 initiative. Friend in Every Town (Social): +1 trait bonus on Diplomacy and Knowledge (local) checks; Diplomacy is always a class skill.</p><p>Feats (8 regular: the SRD feat at L1/3/5/7 plus the GM&#x27;s extra feat at the same levels; 2 archetype teamwork bonus feats; 2 combat style; regular picks are proposed):</p><p>Regular:</p><ul><li>L1 Weapon Finesse</li><li>L1 Improved Unarmed Strike</li><li>L3 Two-Weapon Fighting</li><li>L3 Weapon Focus (unarmed strike)</li><li>L5 Open (feat to be chosen later)</li><li>L5 Open (feat to be chosen later)</li><li>L7 Improved Two-Weapon Fighting</li><li>L7 Expanded Arcana (adds 1 spell known: detonate, 4th level)</li></ul><p>Archetype feats (Companion-Bound Ranger, Teamwork, 4th level):</p><ul><li>L4 Coordinated Companion (Teamwork): gives her panther any teamwork feat she has (within 30 ft, and it must see or hear her).</li><li>L4 Bonded Mind (Teamwork): while she and an ally with the feat can see each other, they trade silent messages as the message spell, with no whispering or pointing, and nobody can overhear. The panther can use it with her.</li></ul><p>Companion-Bound Ranger replaces Endurance (3rd), favored terrain, hunter&#x27;s bond (4th), woodland stride (7th) and, later, hunter&#x27;s camouflage. It leaves her favored enemies and her combat style alone.</p><p>Combat style feats (Unarmed, prerequisites waived):</p><ul><li>L2 Monastic Legacy</li><li>L6 Stunning Fist</li></ul><p>Ranger talents:</p><ul><li>L4 Skirmishing Attack</li><li>L7 Improved Stealth Attack (+1d6 stealth attack)</li></ul><p>Mythic feat:</p><ul><li>Tier 1 Mythic Spell Lore: she learns mythic spells equal to her tier (2 now, +1 per tier) and can spend mythic power when casting them. Mythic spells: fireball and dimension door (see the Mythic section).</li></ul>", "ranger": "<p>Spell-less Ranger 8 (Companion-Bound Ranger archetype):</p><ul><li>Favored enemy: humanoid (elf, covers drow) (+4, first), undead (+2, second). Bonus on weapon attack and damage, and on Bluff, Knowledge, Perception, Sense Motive, Survival checks against them.</li><li>Single favored terrain (Companion-Bound; replaces favored terrain): forest, +2 at 3rd level and +4 at 8th. Bonus on initiative, Knowledge (geography), Perception, Stealth, Survival in that terrain. No more terrains as she levels; the bonus just grows. Underground is no longer a favored terrain, though drow stay a favored enemy.</li><li>Proficiencies: all simple and martial weapons (ranger), light and medium armor, shields except tower shields. Eternal Mage adds nothing (simple weapons, no armor). Her unarmed strikes are armed with Improved Unarmed Strike.</li><li>Fast Movement (5th): +10 ft base speed in a favored terrain, only in light, medium or no armor. Speed is 35 ft (30 elf + 5 Wanderer&#x27;s Stride), 45 ft in forest.</li><li>Track: add half her level (+4) to Survival checks to follow or identify tracks. Swift Tracker (8th): she moves at normal speed while tracking without the -5 penalty, and takes only -10 (not -20) at up to twice normal speed.</li><li>Wild Empathy: +14 (8 + Cha 6), +18 with her animal companion; works within 30 ft.</li><li>Nature&#x27;s Healing (3rd): +2 on Heal checks in a favored terrain (Heal +8, or +10 in forest). In forest she also gets long-term care (3 hp per character level for 8 hours of rest, or 6 for a full day; the same for ability damage), treat deadly wounds with an extra 1d6 + 1 hp per 3 levels and no healer&#x27;s kit needed, and +8 on the patient&#x27;s save when her Heal check beats a poison or disease DC by 5.</li><li>Stealth attack 3d6 (2d6 base +1d6 Improved Stealth Attack; see weapon lines above). It applies when the target is denied its Dex bonus or flanked, only in a favored terrain or against a favored enemy, only while she wears light, medium or no armor, and the extra damage is not multiplied on a critical hit. Ranged attacks count only within 30 ft. Style feats also work only in light or medium armor or none.</li><li>Animal companion (Companion-Bound, 3rd; replaces Endurance): panther (any animal on the druid list is allowed), effective druid level 8. +4 on wild empathy and Handle Animal checks with it (Handle Animal +21). It shares her favored enemy and favored terrain bonuses.</li><li>Enhanced Companion (7th; replaces woodland stride): she gains a bonus feat of her own from Greater Animal Companion, Improved Animal Companion, Increased Devotion or Invulnerable Animal Companion (these feats are taken by the ranger and improve the panther), or instead an Animal Feat chosen for the panther. Taken: Improved Animal Companion. Gwathfaron gains +1d8 hp (50 total), +1 Dex (22) and +2 natural armor (AC 23); see his tab. The archetype lists this feat and gives her the animal companion, so its hunter&#x27;s bond/nature&#x27;s bond prerequisite is met. Greater Animal Companion (it needs Improved Animal Companion) and Invulnerable Animal Companion come later.</li></ul>", "mage": "<p>Eternal Mage 8 (Artillery Expert archetype):</p><ul><li>Eternal spellcasting (Cha-based). No spell slots and no preparation. Limited only by eldritch burnout and limited concentration. Needs Cha 10 + spell level to learn or cast a spell.</li><li>Artillery Adept (1st): free arcane artillery secret, costs no overdrive (the GM allows her to keep her cantrips). Artillery Overdrive (2nd): 1 overdrive turns d6 into d8.</li><li>Arcane overdrive pool: 10 points (Cha 6 + half level 4). 1 point ignores up to 4 burnout from a spell. Refills after 8 hours of sleep.</li><li>Eternal secrets (3rd, 6th): Artillery Burst, Artillery Sniper.</li><li>Arcane buffer 2 (4th, 8th): every spell gives 2 less burnout.</li><li>School focus: Evocation, Abjuration, Transmutation, plus an additional school at 5th: Conjuration (proposed).</li><li>Experimental spell (6th). Expanded concentration (7th): she can keep 2 spells with a duration active at once. Casting a third ends the older one.</li></ul>", "mythic": "<p>Mythic: Archmage, Tier 2. Mythic power 3 + 2/tier = 7 per day.</p><p>Base mythic abilities:</p><ul><li>Ability score (Tier 2): +2 Int (16 to 18), already counted above.</li><li>Mythic feat (Tier 1): Mythic Spell Lore (replaces Weapon Finesse (Mythic)): mythic spells fireball and dimension door. The next mythic feat comes at Tier 3.</li><li>Mythic spells (Mythic Spell Lore; she must be able to cast the non-mythic spell, and both are on her spells known):</li><li>Fireball (mythic): damage becomes 1d10 fire per caster level, maximum 10d10. A creature that fails its Reflex save also catches fire, taking 2d6 fire each round until put out (extinguishing uses the spell&#x27;s save DC). With Elemental Bond her caster level is 10, so 10d10 (average 55) against 10d6 (35). Augmented (6th) needs Mythic Tier 6, so she cannot cast it at Tier 2. Later it costs 2 mythic power in total (the 1 for the mythic version included): maximum damage 20d10, area becomes a 40 ft radius spread, and the fire damage ignores fire resistance and immunity.</li><li>Dimension door (mythic): the spell&#x27;s duration is 1 round per 2 caster levels and it creates a temporary invisible one-way portal in her square, which she passes through at once. She cannot take other creatures, but she can designate a number of creatures equal to her caster level (8) who can see and use the portal (passing through is not an action). A creature that passes through cannot take other actions until its next turn. The full spell entry has no augmented line. Mythic version: she goes through at once and cannot bring anyone herself; the designated creatures use the portal instead.</li><li>Cost: casting a mythic spell costs 1 mythic power (the mythic spell rules; an augmented version&#x27;s cost includes that 1). The number in parentheses on an augmented entry is the mythic tier needed to use it. The version is chosen when the spell is cast. Both spells were checked against the d20pfsrd text you pasted.</li><li>Hard to Kill (Ex): below 0 hit points she stabilizes automatically, and she dies only at negative hit points equal to or greater than double her Con score (32). Bleed damage still hurts.</li><li>Mythic power (Su): 7 uses a day (3 + 2 x tier). Each of these costs 1: Surge, the extra action from Amazing Initiative, Wild Arcana, and casting a mythic spell (fireball, dimension door).</li><li>Surge (Su): 1 mythic power, immediate action, add 1d6 to a d20 roll she just made, after seeing the result (1d8 at Tier 4).</li><li>Amazing Initiative (Ex, Tier 2): +2 on initiative (her tier). Once per round as a free action on her turn she may spend 1 mythic power to take an extra standard action that turn. It cannot be used to cast a spell, so no artillery or spells.</li><li>Archmage Arcana (Tier 1): Wild Arcana. As a standard action spending 1 mythic power she can cast any one arcane spell without it being known, and her caster level counts as 2 higher for level-dependent effects. Burnout still applies. (Mythic Adventures FAQ: standard action, not swift.) It is not an Eternal Mage mechanic, so her focus schools do not restrict it.</li><li>Path ability, Tier 1: Eldritch Breach (Su, passive). When she rolls a caster level check to dispel, to overcome spell resistance, or to see whether her magic affects a target, she rolls twice and takes the higher result.</li><li>Path ability, Tier 2: Elemental Bond (Su), fire. Spells with the fire descriptor get her tier (+2) added to caster level, so fireball is 10d6 and scorching ray is cast at CL 10. She also has fire resistance 10 (20 at Tier 6, 30 at Tier 9). Detonate (Evocation [acid, cold, electricity or fire]) counts only when she casts it as fire; then it is 10d8.</li></ul>", "spells": "<p>(D) = a spell with a duration other than instantaneous or permanent. Only 2 of these can be active at once (limited concentration; expanded concentration at 7th). Casting a third ends the older one.</p><p>0 (8 known, no burnout): acid splash, ray of frost, spark, mage hand (D), message (D), mending, open/close, prestidigitation (D)</p><p>Racial light or dancing lights 1/day, no burnout. It counts as one of her 2 active duration spells while it lasts.</p><p>1: shield (D), expeditious retreat (D), feather fall (D), magic missile, blood money</p><p>2: darkvision (D), resist energy (D), scorching ray</p><p>3: dispel magic, fireball</p><p>4: dimension door, detonate (from Expanded Arcana)</p><p>Durations at CL 8: shield and expeditious retreat 8 min, feather fall 8 rounds (or until she lands), darkvision 8 hours, resist energy 80 min, message 80 min, prestidigitation 1 hour, mage hand while she concentrates, haste (experimental) 8 rounds. Mythic dimension door lasts 4 rounds (1 round per 2 levels), so it counts as a (D) spell while the portal is open.</p><p>Blood Money (Transmutation 1, wizard/sorcerer, magus, witch; Rise of the Runelords Anniversary Edition on d20pfsrd; swift action, V S, personal, effect 1 material component, instantaneous): cast just before another spell. &quot;As part of this spell&#x27;s casting, you must cut one of your hands, releasing a stream of blood ... that causes you to take 1d6 points of damage.&quot; When she casts another spell that round, the blood becomes one material component. Components worth more than 1 gp &quot;requires an additional cost of 1 point of Strength damage, plus a further point of damage for every full 500 gp of the component&#x27;s value.&quot; An unused component turns back into blood at the end of the round. Detonate&#x27;s 50 gp vials therefore cost 1d6 damage and 1 Strength damage per cast, and she saves 50 gp of vials. Burnout 0 (level 1, minus 2).</p><p>Detonate (Evocation, 4th, 30 ft radius spread centered on her, V S M 50 gp of acid and alkali vials per cast, Reflex half DC 20, SR yes): she chooses acid, cold, electricity or fire. The blast goes off 1 round after casting: 8d8 within 15 ft, half from 15 to 30 ft. She takes half the damage with no save, and her energy resistance (resist energy gives 20 at CL 8) can cancel it. Burnout 2. It hits allies within 30 ft too.</p><p>Fireball: 10d6 fire with Elemental Bond (CL 10; 8d6 without), 20 ft radius spread, Reflex DC 19 for half. Dimension door: teleports her and objects up to her max load, plus one willing Medium or smaller creature per 3 caster levels (2 at CL 8), range 400 ft + 40 ft/level (720 ft), 2 burnout; she cannot act again until her next turn. Both fireball and dimension door are mythic spells (Mythic Spell Lore): see the Mythic section.</p><p>Experimental spell (6th level, swap each day, +1 burnout): default haste (3rd, 8 rounds). Other days: fly, cat&#x27;s grace, mirror image, protection from energy, protection from evil, or any wizard/sorcerer spell up to 3rd level (any school). It must be below the highest level she can cast (4th), so 3rd or lower.</p><p>Swap: at 8th level she may trade one spell known for another of the same level (one swap per level).</p><p>Typical pairs: shield + resist energy to hold a line; haste (experimental) + shield to fight; expeditious retreat + feather fall to break away; blood money + detonate to pay for the vials; dimension door for a hard escape.</p><p>Armor: the mithral chain shirt gives 10% arcane spell failure on spells with a somatic component (shield, detonate, blood money and others).</p><p>Eldritch burnout: casting a spell of 1st level or higher adds burnout equal to its level, minus 2 for arcane buffer (minimum 0), +1 for the experimental spell. Arcane artillery counts as a 4th-level spell: 2 burnout each shot.</p><ul><li>Spells: 1st and 2nd level 0, 3rd level 1, 4th level 2, experimental +1 (haste: 2). Cantrips 0.</li><li>Each burnout point: -1 caster level. Each 2 points: -1 DC, and -1d6 artillery damage.</li><li>At caster level 0 she can use only cantrips.</li><li>She recovers 1 burnout at the end of any round in which she gains none.</li><li>Overdrive: 1 point (free action) ignores up to 4 burnout from one spell. The artillery overdrive (d6 to d8) is a separate 1-point spend, so a d8 shot with no burnout costs 2 overdrive.</li></ul>", "daily": "<ul><li>Arcane overdrive: 10 points (refills after 8 hours of sleep)</li><li>Mythic power: 7 uses a day</li><li>Stunning Fist: 2 uses a day (1 per round)</li><li>Racial light or dancing lights: 1 a day</li><li>Detonate vials: 2 casts (100 gp of vials; 1 Strength damage per cast if paid with blood money)</li><li>Consumables: 4 potions of cure light wounds, 2 alchemist&#x27;s fire, 2 smokesticks, 1 tanglefoot bag, 2 thunderstones, 5 flasks of oil</li></ul>", "gear": "<p>MONEY: 100 gp 9 cp (of 33,000 gp)</p><p>GEAR (Weight):</p><p>Worn: +1 mithral chain shirt (12.5), +1 bodywrap of mighty strikes (1), cloak of resistance +3, a hooded moon-gray cloak (1), belt of incredible dexterity (1), headband of alluring charisma (1), amulet of natural armor (0), silver eight-pointed star pin (0).</p><p>Handy haversack (5 lb however full; central pack holds 80 lb / 8 cu ft, each of the two side pouches 20 lb / 2 cu ft). Contents about 90.5 lb:</p><p>Camp and travel (38 lb, 15.81 gp)</p><ul><li>bedroll: 5 lb, 1 sp</li><li>winter blanket: 3 lb, 5 sp</li><li>cold-weather outfit: 7 lb, 8 gp</li><li>waterskin: 4 lb, 1 gp</li><li>7 days trail rations: 7 lb, 3 gp 5 sp</li><li>hemp rope, 50 ft: 10 lb, 1 gp</li><li>flint and steel: no weight, 1 gp</li><li>mess kit: 1 lb, 2 sp</li><li>soap: 0.5 lb, 1 cp</li><li>waterproof bag: 0.5 lb, 5 sp</li></ul><p>Light and tools (35.5 lb, 142 gp)</p><ul><li>hooded lantern: 2 lb, 7 gp</li><li>5 flasks of oil: 5 lb, 5 sp</li><li>4 sunrods: 4 lb, 8 gp</li><li>10 candles: no weight, 1 sp</li><li>10 pieces of chalk: no weight, 1 sp</li><li>crowbar: 5 lb, 2 gp</li><li>hammer: 2 lb, 5 sp</li><li>10 pitons: 5 lb, 1 gp</li><li>grappling hook: 4 lb, 1 gp</li><li>climber&#x27;s kit: 5 lb, 80 gp</li><li>thieves&#x27; tools: 1 lb, 30 gp</li><li>small steel mirror: 0.5 lb, 10 gp</li><li>signal whistle: no weight, 8 sp</li><li>caltrops: 2 lb, 1 gp</li></ul><p>Healing and alchemy (12 lb, 290 gp; potions are counted under magic items)</p><ul><li>healer&#x27;s kit: 1 lb, 50 gp</li><li>antitoxin: no weight, 50 gp</li><li>4 potions of cure light wounds: 2 lb, 200 gp (magic items)</li><li>2 alchemist&#x27;s fire: 2 lb, 40 gp</li><li>2 smokesticks: 1 lb, 40 gp</li><li>tanglefoot bag: 4 lb, 50 gp</li><li>2 thunderstones: 2 lb, 60 gp</li></ul><p>Writing and spellcasting (4 lb, 127.1 gp)</p><ul><li>ink vial: no weight, 8 gp</li><li>ink pen: no weight, 1 sp</li><li>10 sheets of paper: no weight, 4 gp</li><li>journal, 50 pages: 1 lb, 10 gp</li><li>spell component pouch: 2 lb, 5 gp</li><li>detonate vials, 2 casts: 1 lb, 100 gp</li></ul><p>Faith (1 lb, 25 gp)</p><ul><li>silver holy symbol of Sehanine: 1 lb, 25 gp</li></ul><p>TOTAL WEIGHT: 21.5 lbs (haversack contents add nothing)</p><p>LOAD:  Light 76 lb   Medium (-3) 153 lb   Heavy/Max (-6) 230 lb   Lift (x 2) 460 lb   Push/Drag (x 5) 1150 lb</p><p>Carrying 21.5 lb: light load</p><h4>MAGIC ITEMS</h4><p>+1 mithral chain shirt (2,100 gp)</p><p>+1 bodywrap of mighty strikes (3,000 gp)</p><p>Cloak of resistance +3 (9,000 gp)</p><p>Belt of incredible dexterity +2 (4,000 gp)</p><p>Headband of alluring charisma +2 (4,000 gp)</p><p>Amulet of natural armor +2 (8,000 gp)</p><p>Handy haversack (2,000 gp)</p><p>4 potions of cure light wounds (200 gp)</p>", "lang": "<p>Languages (11): Common, Elven, Sylvan, Orc, Goblin, Draconic, Gnoll, Celestial, Dwarven, Undercommon, Gnome</p>", "bg": "<p>Daerlieth is tall and lean even for an elf, with the long-fingered, quick hands of a lifelong skirmisher. Ivory-white skin with blue tints, silver-white hair with a faint blue sheen worn in a loose braid, blue eyes with gold flecks. She dresses for the road in a mithral chain shirt under a hooded moon-gray cloak, with her family&#x27;s eight-pointed silver star on a simple pin. She never looks hurried, but her eyes are always moving, tracking the tree line, the exits and the people who aren&#x27;t talking. No staff, wand or spellbook, which unsettles Cormanthyr&#x27;s mages.</p><h4>BACKGROUND</h4><p>House Nightstar (Teu&#x27;Tel&#x27;Quessir). Moon elf of a minor line. At twenty she cast her first spell untaught, and her magic has never needed a spellbook, preparation or prayer. Her aunt Gweyr, the house archmage, found no discipline in it, and the wizards called her lazy. She left for the border woods and spent decades with the green elf scouts, learning to track, fight bare-handed and live off the land, then returned to the City of Song as a ranger who can hurl raw arcane force. Her grandfather Seith, advisor to the Harpers at Twilight, recommended her for the Coronal&#x27;s Defenders. Panther companion Gwathfaron (Sindarin, &quot;shadow hunter&quot;); scout mentor: name not yet chosen.</p>"};})();
